// Forwarding is po-forward (#210).
//
// The source of a forwarding is po-before the event it replaces: a read is
// never satisfied from a store po-after it. Forwarding x := 1 into r1 would
// give r1 = 1, which no model of a single thread allows. The store to y puts
// both in the window of a justified write.
x := 0; y := 0;
r1 := x;
x := 1;
y := r1;
%%
forbid (r1 = 1) [sMRD, RC11]
